.Rproj.user
.Rhistory
.RData
.Ruserdata
DTAtools.Rproj
inst/doc
testdata
/doc/
/Meta/
example/
*Rproj
# Anchored to the repo root: this ignores a root-level scratch file only. Left
# bare it would match at any depth and silently untrack tests/testthat/helper.R,
# testthat's canonical helper filename.
/helper.R
renv/library
renv/staging
renv/settings.json
.Renviron
*docx
# Keep the bundled numbered Word reference template used by the built-in
# write_dta() DOCX/PDF writer (a required package asset, not a scratch export).
!inst/extdata/templates/dta_numbered_template.docx
.tmp*
..Rcheck/00check.log
instructions_shiny.txt
DTATOOLSR_METADATA_IMPLEMENTATION.md
bla.md
test_comprehensive.md
test_output.md
Rplots.pdf
IMPLEMENTATION_TECHNICAL_DETAILS.md
CLAUDE.local.md
.claude/settings.local.json
graphify-out/
.claude/cache/

# Private templates (see vignette("private-templates")) carry real supplier/
# receiver names and contacts, and must never be committable to this
# open-source repository by accident: a project-local template checkout, and
# any party-profile file authored outside the package's own worked examples.
dta-templates/
*.dta-party.yaml
# ...except the packaged, anonymised worked examples under
# inst/extdata/templates/ and the starter set create_template_repo() copies
# from inst/extdata/template-repo-skeleton/, which are shipped package data,
# not private information -- keep them trackable.
#
# Forgetting the second of these is not a cosmetic mistake: the file stays on
# disk, so pkgload::load_all() and the whole local test suite keep passing
# while the BUILT package ships a skeleton whose creation template references
# a party profile that is not there. That reached CI as a party_slot_invalid
# failure on all five platforms and nothing before it.
!inst/extdata/templates/*.dta-party.yaml
!inst/extdata/template-repo-skeleton/*.dta-party.yaml
